From 1a1eda691766f6f87add08e691470e0c528a0e88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis James <travis@tribehealthsolutions.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:45:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(runtimes): support OpenCode 2.x CLI alongside 1.x
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OpenCode 2.0 removed `--dir`, `--pure`, `--variant` and
`--dangerously-skip-permissions` from `opencode run`, so every launch
(Settings → OpenCode → Test, chat runs, the memory extractor, child
evidence export) failed with "Unrecognized flag" on 2.x installs.

The daemon now derives the CLI generation from the existing
`run --help` capability probe (`--dir` present → 1.x, absent → 2.x) and
builds the matching argv:

- 1.x keeps `--dangerously-skip-permissions --dir <cwd> [-m m --variant v]`
  and `export <id> --sanitize --pure`, byte-for-byte unchanged.
- 2.x sends `--auto --standalone [-m model#variant]`, pins `PWD` to the
  project directory for the 2.0.x builds that consulted it, lists models
  with plain `models` when `--verbose` is rejected, and exports through
  `session export <id> --sanitize --standalone`.
- Connection test and memory extractor warm the capability probe before
  building argv; the probe cache keys on the binary's size and mtime so
  an in-place upgrade re-probes, and an empty probe result is not cached.
- The outdated-CLI hint no longer tells a 2.x user to upgrade when the
  flag mismatch is on OpenDesign's side.
